# Read by ripgrep, and by the search tools of hosts that are built on it, in whatever tree
# holds this skill folder. A project install puts the skill inside the repository being
# triaged (<repository>/.claude/skills/report-triage, <repository>/.agents/skills/...),
# and a search of that repository would return lines from it. Measured with the skills
# then installed for two hosts: a hidden-aware search for a C library function returned
# 12 files of this skill and 44 of the skills together, against 1 of the product.
#
# This hides nothing from a person or from a model that opens a file by its path. It keeps
# the skill's own text, which carries the vocabulary of the report being checked, out of
# searches of the code under review:
#   references/   the contract, the role files, the limits
#   scripts/      the tools, whose source holds the probe's word lists, and the self-test
# SKILL.md stays visible. The patterns are anchored to the skill folder, so a `scripts/` of
# the repository under review is still searched.
# To search the skill itself, ask for it: rg --no-ignore PATTERN <skill folder>.
/references/
/scripts/
